
Run the desktop C++ tests from the project root:

    python3 scripts/test_led_sectors.py

Requires Python 3 and a C++11 compiler (c++ by default; override with CXX).
No ESP32 libraries or hardware are needed.

test_led_sectors.cpp exercises the same led-sectors.h helper used by main.cpp:
single-pass compatibility, repeated ratios and multiple colours, ring clipping,
empty/zero/negative patterns, and counts too large for the ring. The runner
imposes a timeout to catch nonterminating patterns.

Both CI and release workflows run these tests before compiling the firmware.
